## Memory discipline

1. **Project truth** (committed, human-gated): `project/global/state.md`.
2. **Working memory** (committed, rewritten often): `project/<author>/session.md`
   and `project/global/method_spec.md`.
3. **Records** (committed, append-only): `project/<author>/logs/runs.jsonl` —
   one line per script execution, tying a number to the run that produced it.
4. **Working material** (local, gitignored): the briefs sent to each seat and
   `project/<author>/logs/debate-<run>.jsonl`,
   the full model responses. Read a slice when a question needs one; never read
   it forward as context.

Tiers 1 and 2 are what you carry between sessions; 3 and 4 are what you go back
to when something has to be reconstructed. Rewrite tiers 1 and 2 compactly;
never append forever. A file that accumulates
superseded blocks under a "this is all stale now" banner is worse than useless —
it reads as current. When a result is superseded, cut it to a line saying so and
where the truth now lives.

